# The ignore file of docker/Dockerfile (BuildKit reads `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` beside the Dockerfile before the one at the root). The context is the
# repository root, and an ALLOW LIST: only what the two cargo builds read goes into the build stage. A file that is missing fails the build, loudly.
#
# Why it matters: a build from a working tree would otherwise send `target/` (gigabytes) and `.git`, and `COPY . .` would make a change under web/ or
# docs/ rebuild the compile layer. A CI checkout's context is 76 MB, 55 MB of it web/ (measured 2026-11-23).
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!.cargo
!crates

# Inside the allowed directories, what a working tree grows that a build must not read or send (the last match wins, so these come after the allow list).
**/target
**/node_modules
**/.wrangler
**/mutants.out*
**/.env*
**/.dev.vars*
